From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:38:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 153/159] arm64: dts: qcom: nairo: Set the battery ESR

The fuel gauge corrects the OCV for the drop across the battery's
internal resistance. Downstream learns it at runtime; use the voltage
drop per ampere measured on this phone at about 95% charge, connector
and sense path included: 220 mOhm.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
index bd1b90463e12..eeaba233d9a7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
@@ -120,6 +120,12 @@ battery: battery {
 		compatible = "simple-battery";
 		charge-full-design-microamp-hours = <5000000>;
 		voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3200000>;
+		/*
+		 * Downstream learns the battery resistance at runtime; this is
+		 * the voltage drop per ampere measured at about 95% charge,
+		 * connector and sense path included.
+		 */
+		factory-internal-resistance-micro-ohms = <220000>;
 
 		/* qcom,lz50-amperex-5000mah qcom,pc-temp-v2-lut, from the downstream DT */
 		ocv-capacity-celsius = <(-10) (0) (10) (25) (40) (50)>;
